{
  "what": "a Tier 3 reconstruction of all 30 clips from the released video alone, put into the released world frame and scored against Tier 1 truth",
  "pipeline": "NVIDIA's own reconstruction modules, in their intended order: v2d_geocalib -> v2d_moge (depth + intrinsics) -> v2d_grounding_dino (detect the named object) -> a prompt converter -> v2d_sam2 (masks) -> v2d_foundation_pose (6-DoF pose per frame, nvlabs_pytorch backend). MegaPose was the original plan and was abandoned: its only weight host is unreachable and every mirror probed 403s or 404s.",
  "alignment": "ONE rigid transform from frame 0, as the FAQ permits (nvidia-isaac/video_to_data PR 207: 'teams may use the first frame of Tier 1 data to compute alignment'). world_T_cam = world_T_obj[0] @ inv(cam_T_obj[0]), applied unchanged to every later frame. No scale fitted, no per-frame correction, nothing after frame 0 read from Tier 1. Frame-0 position residual 0.0000 cm and orientation residual 0.000 deg on all 30 clips, which is also the check that the wxyz quaternion convention is right -- Transform3d is imported from upstream rather than reimplemented.",
  "object_identity": "read from meta/episodes_metadata.jsonl (the 'object'/'mesh' fields only, never 'task'), because the object cannot be derived from the sequence id: e05 is 'g1_box_rotate_01' whose mesh is 'big_black_box'.",
  "overall_kit_score_of_the_raw_reconstruction": {
    "add_auc": 0.22799019040404067,
    "maniptrans_sr": 0.03333333333333333,
    "mppe_cm": 66.60263222640054,
    "spider_sr": 0.3333333333333333
  },
  "frames_scored": 22989,
  "quality": "sharply bimodal rather than uniformly mediocre. 10 clips track well (<5 deg mean orientation drift and <16 cm mean position error): e00, e08, e18, e20, e21, e22, e23, e24, e26, e29. The other 20 lose the object and run to tens of centimetres or metres.",
  "tracked_well": [
    "e00",
    "e08",
    "e18",
    "e20",
    "e21",
    "e22",
    "e23",
    "e24",
    "e26",
    "e29"
  ],
  "can_the_raw_reconstruction_be_submitted_as_is": "No, not honestly. The kit's packer accepts an empty checkpoint_sha256 but requires a non-empty, uniform eval_code_sha256 (tools/pack_submission.py:420-445). A reconstruction is not an evaluator run, so there is no honest value for that field, and inventing one is the exact misrepresentation src/v2d/submit/tier1.py's NOT_FOR_SUBMISSION guard exists to prevent. The tier's own input_note says to 'drive your policy from that', so the entry has to be a policy rollout against this reconstruction -- which also supplies real provenance.",
  "next": "free: retarget all 30 clips against these object trajectories (v2d retarget --object-npz) to get whole-body references the evaluator can drive; then one eval-only box (~$1) rolling the 30 shipped actors out against them; then pack, validate, submit. Expect a score well below the 0.228 the raw reconstruction scores, because driving an actor with a reference it never trained on costs it a lot -- measured, not guessed: results/t1_clean_input_eval.json.",
